// THE DISPATCHER (owner ruling 2026-07-25 — "um tkp pode ter vários tkr … somente um build é
// necessário"; and "está proibido inline code em tkr"): this project hosts its OWN regression and
// the scenarios unfolded out of regressor.tkr's `Given source inline` blocks — one MEMBER NAMESPACE
// each under `src/`. `TEKO_REGR_ENTRY` selects which member's `entry()` runs, and every member runs
// off THIS project's SINGLE build (`RegrBuilt` compiles a project's `.tkp` at most once per `.tkr`).
// It is the same selector the synthesized group builds use (`REGR_GROUP_ENTRY_VAR`,
// src/build/regr_group.tks), so an on-disk member and a folded snippet are selected identically.
//
// `regr_hit` is why the `exit(0)` below is not dead code, and it is not cosmetic: a member's body is
// a virtual main, and a virtual main that simply RUNS OFF THE END exits 0. Without the flag such a
// member would fall through into this project's own body and report ITS exit code instead — which
// is exactly the bug this dispatcher was first written with, caught by the gate. With no selector
// set, `regr_hit` stays false and the project's own scenario runs, unchanged.
